ns. In a previous paper (2000, Amer. J. Math.122, 637–666), we studied an intermediate, and perhaps more natural, condition: purely infinite, that extends a well known property for simple C*-algebras. The weakest condition of the three, weakly purely infinite, is shown to be equivalent to the absence of quasitraces in an ultrapower of the C*-algebra. The three conditions may be equivalent for all C*-algebras, and we prove this to be the case for C*-algebras that are either simple, of real rank zero, or approximately divisible.},
