	doi = {10.1007/s00023-010-0034-7},
	abstract = {Let T be an aperiodic and repetitive tiling of Rd\{\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathbb R\}ˆd\} with finite local complexity. Let Ω be its tiling space with canonical transversal Ξ\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} . The tiling equivalence relation RΞ\{R\_{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} is the set of pairs of tilings in Ξ\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} which are translates of each others, with a certain (étale) topology. In this paper RΞ\{R\_{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} is reconstructed as a generalized “tail equivalence” on a Bratteli diagram, with its standard AF -relation as a subequivalence relation. Using a generalization of the Anderson–Putnam complex (Bellissard et al. in Commun. Math. Phys. 261:1–41, 2006) Ω is identified with the inverse limit of a sequence of finite CW-complexes. A Bratteli diagram B\{\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal B\}\} is built from this sequence, and its set of infinite paths ∂B\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashpartial \{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal B\}\} is homeomorphic to Ξ\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} . The diagram B\{\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal B\}\} is endowed with a horizontal structure: additional edges that encode the adjacencies of patches in T. This allows to define an étale equivalence relation RB\{R\_\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal B\}\} on ∂B\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashpartial \{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal B\}\} which is homeomorphic to RΞ\{R\_{\textbackslash}textbackslashXi\} , and contains the AF-relation of “tail equivalence”.},
	
