	abstract = {For \$d = 2, 3, {\textbackslash}textbackslashldots\$ and \$p {\textbackslash}textbackslashin [1, {\textbackslash}textbackslashinfty),\$ we define a class of representations \${\textbackslash}textbackslashrho\$ of the Leavitt algebra \$L\_d\$ on spaces of the form \$Lˆp (X, {\textbackslash}textbackslashmu),\$ which we call the spatial representations. We prove that for fixed \$d\$ and \$p,\$ the Banach algebra \$\{\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal\{O\}\}\_\{d\}ˆ\{p\}\}\$ obtained as the closure of the image of \$L\_d\$ under the representation \${\textbackslash}textbackslashrho\$ is the same for all spatial representations \${\textbackslash}textbackslashrho.\$ When \$p = 2,\$ we recover the usual Cuntz algebra \$\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal\{O\}\}\_\{d\}.\$ We give a number of equivalent conditions for a representation to be spatial. We show that for distinct \$p\_1\$ and \$p\_2\$ in \$[1, {\textbackslash}textbackslashinfty)\$ and arbitrary \$d\_1\$ and \$d\_2\$ in \${\textbackslash}textbackslash\{ 2, 3, {\textbackslash}textbackslashldots {\textbackslash}textbackslash\},\$ there is no nonzero continuous homomorphism from \$\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal\{O\}\}\_\{d\_1\}ˆ\{p\_1\}\$ to \$\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathcal\{O\}\}\_\{d\_2\}ˆ\{p\_2\}.\$},
