	abstract = {We investigate some subtle and interesting phenomena in the duality theory of operator spaces and operator algebras, and give several applications of the surprising fact that certain maps are always weak**-continuous on dual spaces. In particular, if X is a subspace of a C*C*-algebra A , and if a∈Aa∈A satisfies aX⊂XaX⊂X, then we show that the function x↦axx↦ax on X is automatically weak** continuous if either (a) X is a dual operator space, or (b) a*X⊂Xa*X⊂X and X is a dual Banach space. These results hinge on a generalization to Banach modules of Tomiyama's famous theorem on contractive projections onto a C*C*-subalgebra. Applications include a new characterization of the σσ-weakly closed (possibly nonunital and nonselfadjoint) operator algebras, and a generalization of the theory of W*W*-modules to the framework of modules over such algebras. We also give a Banach module characterization of σσ-weakly closed spaces of operators which are invariant under the action of a von Neumann algebra.},
