	abstract = {A (finite or countably infinite) set G of generators of an abstract C*-algebra A is called hyperrigid if for every faithful representation of A on a Hilbert space A ⊆ B(H) and every sequence of unital completely positive linear maps ϕ 1, ϕ 2,... from B(H) to itself, limn→∞{\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbarϕn(g)−g{\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbar=0,∀g∈G⇒limn→∞ϕn(a)−a{\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbar=0,∀a∈A.{\textbackslash}textbackslashmathop \{{\textbackslash}textbackslashlim \}{\textbackslash}textbackslashlimits\_\{n {\textbackslash}textbackslashto {\textbackslash}textbackslashinfty \} {\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbar\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashphi \_n\}(g) - g{\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbar = 0,\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashforall \_g\} {\textbackslash}textbackslashin G {\textbackslash}textbackslashRightarrow {\textbackslash}textbackslashmathop \{{\textbackslash}textbackslashlim \}{\textbackslash}textbackslashlimits\_\{n {\textbackslash}textbackslashto {\textbackslash}textbackslashinfty \} \{{\textbackslash}textbackslashphi \_n\}(a) - a{\textbackslash}textbar{\textbackslash}textbar = 0,\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashforall \_a\} {\textbackslash}textbackslashin A. We show that one can determine whether a given set G of generators is hyperrigid by examining the noncommutative Choquet boundary of the operator space spanned by G ∪ G*. We present a variety of concrete applications and discuss prospects for further development.},
	
