	abstract = {For every countable discrete group \$G\$, we define an action \${\textbackslash}textbackslashgamma\$ of \$G\$ on the Jiang-Su algebra \${\textbackslash}textbackslashZz\$. If the group is elementary amenable, then \${\textbackslash}textbackslashgamma\$ enjoys the weak Rokhlin property. We use \${\textbackslash}textbackslashgamma\$ to show that, when \$G\$ is elementary amenable, there always exists a \$G\$-action \${\textbackslash}textbackslashomega\$ with the tracial Rokhlin property on any unital simple \${\textbackslash}textbackslashZz\$-stable tracially approximately divisible \$Cˆ*\$-algebra \$A\$. For the \${\textbackslash}textbackslashomega\$ we construct, we show that if \$A\$ is unital simple and \${\textbackslash}textbackslashZz\$-stable with rational tracial rank at most one, and \$G\$ belongs to the class of countable discrete groups generated by finite and abelian groups under increasing unions and subgroups, then the crossed product \$A{\textbackslash}textbackslashrtimes\_\{{\textbackslash}textbackslashomega\}G\$ is also unital simple and \${\textbackslash}textbackslashZz\$-stable with rational tracial rank at most one.},
