	abstract = {Milliken-Taylor systems are some of the most general infinitary configurations that are known to be partition regular. These are sets of the form are increasing finite nonempty subsets of , where with and is a sequence in . That is, if is a given linear polynomial and a finite coloring of is given, one gets a sequence such that all sums of the form are monochromatic. In this paper we extend these systems to images of very general extended polynomials. We work with the Stone-Čech compactification of the discrete space of finite subsets of , whose points we take to be the ultrafilters on . We utilize a simply stated result about the tensor products of ultrafilters and the algebraic structure of .},
