	abstract = {Assume that we are given a coaction δ of a locally compact group G on a C ⁎ -algebra A and a T -valued Borel 2-cocycle ω on G. Motivated by the approach of Kasprzak to Rieffelʼs deformation we define a deformation A ω of A. Among other properties of A ω we show that A ω ⊗ K ( L 2 ( G ) ) is canonically isomorphic to A ⋊ δ G ˆ ⋊ δ ˆ , ω G . This, together with a slight extension of a result of Echterhoff et al., implies that for groups satisfying the Baum–Connes conjecture the K-theory of A ω remains invariant under homotopies of ω.},
