	abstract = {.Suppose that X is a topological space with preorder ≦, and that −g, f are bounded upper semicontinuous functions on X such that g(x) ≦ f(y) whenever x ≦ y. We consider the question whether there exists a bounded increasing continuous function h on X such that g ≦ h ≦ f, and obtain an existence theorem that gives necessary and sufficient conditions. This result leads to an extension theorem giving conditions that allow a bounded increasing continuous function defined on an open subset of X to be extended to a function of the same type on X. The application of these results to extremally disconnected locally compact spaces is studied.},
	
